---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/NavBar.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <NavBar />
  <article class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
    <h1 class="mb-2 font-serif text-5xl font-bold">Now</h1>
    <p class="mb-10 text-base text-[#4a4a4a]">What&apos;s AbdulKabir up to?</p>

    <section class="space-y-3" aria-label="Current update">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Jul 20</p>
      <p class="text-[#1a1a1a]">
        I had a lot of fun in July. We went camping, kayaking, canoeing,
        ziplining, challenge course, road trips. I got to work on my car. I
        replaced the two front door speakers, detailed the car myself, fixed my
        car air conditioning, did some scratch buffering. We rearranged the
        house a bit, did a lot of unjustified assembling (sectional couch,
        bedframes, shoe rack, shelves). My wife became a citizen, we had an
        amazing party with familiy and friends. Lots of fun. July was lovely. I
        wouldn&apos;t mind four of this in a year.
      </p>
    </section>

    <details id="now-previous" class="mt-10">
      <summary
        class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-600 transition hover:text-gray-800"
      >
        <span class="now-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Previously…
      </summary>
      <div class="now-previous-timeline">
        <div class="now-previous-entry">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-gray-600">Jun 22</p>
          <p>
            It&apos;s June 22nd and we&apos;re not yet in the summer. I&apos;m
            looking to try out different sports this summer. Two tennis matches
            so far and I love it. This past weekend I participated in a softball
            tournament at work and it was a blast. We didn&apos;t win any match
            but it was super fun. I made an home run. My manager said I brought
            my competitive spirit to the team. Maybe I&apos;ll play more
            softball this summer.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="now-previous-entry">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-gray-600">May 25</p>
          <!-- <p class="mb-2 font-semibold text-[#1a1a1a]">2026 Summer Trip</p> -->
          <p class="mb-3">
            2026 Summer Trip: I had a lovely vacation, visited friends and
            family. Visited Calgary (+ went karting), Minnesota, and the Mall of
            America, Downtown Chicago, from the bean to The Pier. Visited
            Champaign, Illinois for my brother's Ph.D graduation, lots of
            various parties and receptions. Met his friends. Travelled to San
            Francisco, California for Google I/O 2026. Toured around the Google
            Campus, Santa Clara, Mountain View, Menlo Park, Oakland, San
            Francisco and visited the Golden Gate Bridge + Pier 39, sea lions
            and the whole shebang.
            <a
              href="https://dev.to/justcabyr/2026-summer-trip-2amo"
              class="text-orange-600 hover:underline"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Read more
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="now-previous-entry">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-gray-600">Apr 29</p>
          <p>
            I&apos;m refreshing this site, tinkering with Astro, and keeping a
            few side projects moving in small slices. I&apos;ve been reading
            more than I scroll lately, which is a welcome change. Stopped
            drinking coffee and started drinking more water. Decluttering the
            house and reorganizing everything is legit a whole lot of work.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="now-previous-entry">
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm text-gray-600">Jan 20</p>
          <p>
            I started building my social app{' '}
            <a href="/color-lumie" class="text-orange-600 hover:underline"
              >Color Lumie</a
            >—a private space for you and your closest friends to stay connected
            through color instead of feeds. No endless scrolling or public
            profiles: you set your daily Lumie, share your light, and see who
            might need a little extra warmth today.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  #now-previous summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  #now-previous summary {
    list-style: none;
  }

  .now-chevron {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0;
    height: 0;
    border-top: 5px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 5px solid transparent;
    border-left: 7px solid currentColor;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease;
  }

  #now-previous[open] .now-chevron {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  .now-previous-timeline {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 1px solid #d1d5db;
    color: #374151;
  }

  .now-previous-entry {
    position: relative;
  }

  .now-previous-entry:not(:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .now-previous-entry::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(-1.5rem - 4.5px);
    top: 0.375rem;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background-color: #9ca3af;
  }
</style>
